---
import DiagramShell from "./DiagramShell.astro";
---

<DiagramShell
  title="Govern · Authorize · Verify"
  caption="Three functional domains. Authorize owns runtime prevention. Verify is read-only and cannot grant runtime authority. Domain layers do not claim separate physical hosts or networks."
  className="bg-diagram--gav bg-diagram--gav-layered"
>
  <div class="bg-gav bg-gav--layered" role="list">
    <section class="bg-gav-column bg-gav-column--govern" aria-labelledby="gav-govern" role="listitem">
      <p class="bg-gav-kicker">GOVERN</p>
      <h4 id="gav-govern" class="bg-gav-title">Management and release lifecycle</h4>
      <ul class="bg-gav-list">
        <li>Compliance Playbooks</li>
        <li>Validation and approval</li>
        <li>Signing and distribution</li>
        <li>Active Verified Release</li>
        <li>Runtime topology and trust</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gav-column bg-gav-column--authorize" aria-labelledby="gav-authorize" role="listitem">
      <p class="bg-gav-kicker">AUTHORIZE</p>
      <h4 id="gav-authorize" class="bg-gav-title">Runtime authorization domain</h4>
      <ul class="bg-gav-list">
        <li>Request Admission Authorization</li>
        <li>Untrusted AI-generated result</li>
        <li>Declared action</li>
        <li>Result-to-Action Authorization</li>
        <li>Binary ALLOW or DENY</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gav-column bg-gav-column--verify" aria-labelledby="gav-verify" role="listitem">
      <p class="bg-gav-kicker">VERIFY</p>
      <h4 id="gav-verify" class="bg-gav-title">Read-only verification domain</h4>
      <ul class="bg-gav-list">
        <li>Executive Reporting</li>
        <li>Decision Explorer</li>
        <li>Deterministic Reconstruction</li>
        <li>Source Evidence and replay</li>
        <li>Verifiable Export</li>
        <li>AI-Assisted Insights (non-authoritative)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div slot="text">
    <p>
      Govern: management and release lifecycle through an Active Verified
      Release. Authorize: runtime Request Admission Authorization and
      Result-to-Action Authorization with binary ALLOW or DENY. Verify: read-only
      investigation through reporting, Decision Explorer, reconstruction, source
      evidence, replay, export, and non-authoritative AI-assisted insights.
      These are functional domains, not claimed physical separation.
    </p>
  </div>
</DiagramShell>
